    {
     "kind": "debate",
     "text": "The Hebrew word וְר֣וּחַ covers wind, breath and spirit (see its lexicon range). The Septuagint has πνεῦμα and the Vulgate spiritus, both able to mean breath or spirit; WEBC capitalises it as \"Spirit\". Whether the verse speaks of a wind from God or of God's Spirit is a matter of reading.",
