     "kind": "debate",
     "text": "Two nouns stand side by side: בְּצַלְמֵ֖נוּ כִּדְמוּתֵ֑נוּ. The Septuagint renders them εἰκόνα ὁμοίωσιν and the Vulgate imaginem et similitudinem. Whether \"image\" and \"likeness\" name one idea twice or two distinct things has been read both ways.",
